// Read-only lookups, including both approval lookups. These need their own
// permit so that their completed calls are recorded as responses.
permit (
  principal,
  action in [
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_failure_codes",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_my_assigned_workorders",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_schedule_calendar",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_actuals_vs_planned",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_costs",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_kpis",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_tasks",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___list_workorders",
    Drupe::Action::"Dorvane___get_approval",
    Drupe::Action::"Tolvick___get_approval"
  ],
  resource
);

// Close at MAIN, backed by a completed Dorvane lookup within the last hour
// showing an ACCEPTED decision by a PERSON for this exact work order and site.
@id("close_main_with_person_approval_dorvane")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"MaintData___close_workorder", resource)
when { context.input.site_id == "MAIN" }
when temporal {
  formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Dorvane___get_approval"::response{
    eventResource: resource,
    input.wonum: context.input.wonum,
    input.site_id: context.input.site_id,
    output.decision: Drupe::Dorvane___get_approval_Output_decision::"ACCEPTED",
    output.approver_kind: Drupe::Dorvane___get_approval_Output_approver_kind::"PERSON"
  }
};

// Same rule, with a completed Tolvick lookup as the evidence.
@id("close_main_with_person_approval_tolvick")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"MaintData___close_workorder", resource)
when { context.input.site_id == "MAIN" }
when temporal {
  formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Tolvick___get_approval"::response{
    eventResource: resource,
    input.wonum: context.input.wonum,
    input.site_id: context.input.site_id,
    output.decision: "ACCEPTED",
    output.approver_kind: "PERSON"
  }
};
```

Approving, assigning, cancelling, generating and updating work orders have no permit, so they are denied by default.

I made two assumptions:
- The approver's identity is not checked beyond `approver_kind == "PERSON"`.
- Dorvane's `decision` and `approver_kind` are enums, so I matched them with entity literals. Tolvick returns plain strings, so I matched those with string literals.

I did not add a check that an approval was later refused within the hour, since the intent doesn't ask for one.

